WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.624
An expression has structure before we calculate it

00:00:03.624 --> 00:00:09.668
In two plus three times four, the multiplication describes one quantity: three groups of four

00:00:09.668 --> 00:00:14.100
Add the separate two only after finding that product of twelve.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.745
Parentheses change which quantity acts as a factor

00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:24.182
Two plus three now forms one five-object group, and four copies produce twenty

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:29.200
The same symbols can describe a different construction when their grouping changes.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:38.234
Multiplication and division have equal priority, so evaluate them from left to right unless grouping says otherwise

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:47.333
Eighteen divided by three gives six, then multiplying by two gives twelve; multiplying the denominator first would change the expression.

00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:52.383
Nested expressions are read from their inner structure outward

00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:59.467
Square three to get nine, subtract four inside the parentheses to get five, then double the result

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:03.633
A fraction bar also groups its entire numerator and denominator.
